  "prefLabel": "En 1014.02 Applicant Deadlines",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1014.02 Applicant Deadlines.\n\n(a) An applicant may make a request to seek extension of a deadline of the interconnection procedures. Such request shall be in writing.\n\n(b) The utility shall grant an extension request if the applicant demonstrates sufficient justification for the additional extension and the extension duration is reasonable and does not unreasonably delay applications behind the applicant seeking the extension in the queue.\n\n(c) For any missed deadline that would result in an application’s removal from its current queue position, the utility shall notify the applicant a minimum of 8 business days prior to the application being removed from its queue position.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
}
